  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "In the previous chapter, the variance was introduced as a measure of the dispersion of a univariate distribution. Additional statistics are required to describe the joint distribution of two or more variables. The covariance provides a natural measure of the association between two variables, and it appears in the analysis of many problems in quantitative genetics including the resemblance between relatives, the correlation between characters, and measures of selection.",
